# ${{APP_NAME}}

A Rust HTTP server created with Code on the Go, using only `std::net`.

## Run

Tap **Run app** in the editor toolbar, then open
`http://localhost:${{PORT}}` in a browser on the same device. Tap **Cancel Run app**
to stop the server.

| Route | Returns |
|---|---|
| `/` | An HTML page |
| `/api/status` | A JSON status object |

## Test

Tap **Run tests** to run `cargo test`.

## Project structure

```
${{APP_NAME}}/
  Cargo.toml      # package ${{CRATE_NAME}}
  src/
    main.rs       # listener, request handling, and routes
  README.md
```

Each connection is handled on its own thread with read and write timeouts. The
crate uses only the standard library, so it builds and runs with no network
connection.
